<http://data.silknow.org/object/1cb4e471-d3a7-3131-b065-79a516338652/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Wallet or stocking purses were very popular up to the 1860s, and they survive in great numbers, although examples of frame-knitted (machine) purses are rare.  Many stocking purses were netted in silk and had steel beads, spangles and paillettes with steel, gilt, silver or gold sliders and tassels; their decoration varied from the minimal to highly patterned.  Often they were inscribed and dated, many, like this one, were made as gifts for gentlemen."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1cb4e471-d3a7-3131-b065-79a516338652> .

